### Common Pitfalls

**Pitfall 1: Outbox Write Outside Transaction**

```csharp
// ❌ WRONG - Outbox write separate from business transaction
await _dbContext.SaveChangesAsync(); // Business data saved

await _dbContext.Outbox.AddAsync(outboxEvent);
await _dbContext.SaveChangesAsync(); // Outbox event saved separately
// Service crashes between saves - inconsistency!

// ✅ CORRECT - Single transaction for both
using var transaction = await _dbContext.Database.BeginTransactionAsync();
await _dbContext.Claims.AddAsync(claim);
await _dbContext.Outbox.AddAsync(outboxEvent);
await _dbContext.SaveChangesAsync();
await transaction.CommitAsync(); // Both saved atomically
```

**Pitfall 2: Missing Relay Idempotency**

```csharp
// ❌ WRONG - Relay assumes publish succeeds if no exception
await publisher.PublishAsync(event);
outboxEvent.Published = true; // What if this save fails? Event published but not marked!

// ✅ CORRECT - Relay handles duplicate publishes
await publisher.PublishAsync(event);
outboxEvent.Published = true;
await _dbContext.SaveChangesAsync(); // If this fails, event will be published again (idempotent consumers required)
```

**Pitfall 3: Unbounded Outbox Growth**

```csharp
// ❌ WRONG - Never deleting published events causes unbounded growth
// 15K claims/hour = 360K events/day = 131M events/year = multi-TB table

// ✅ CORRECT - Regular cleanup with retention policy
DELETE FROM Outbox
WHERE Published = 1
  AND PublishedAt < DATEADD(day, -7, GETUTCDATE())
```

**Pitfall 4: Polling Without Filtering Index**

```sql
-- ❌ WRONG - Full table scan on every poll
SELECT * FROM Outbox WHERE Published = 0 ORDER BY CreatedAt

-- ✅ CORRECT - Filtered index for efficient relay queries
CREATE INDEX IX_Outbox_Relay ON Outbox (Published, CreatedAt) WHERE Published = 0
```

**Pitfall 5: Synchronous Event Publishing in Transaction**

```csharp
// ❌ WRONG - Publishing to broker inside transaction blocks transaction
using var transaction = await _dbContext.Database.BeginTransactionAsync();
await _dbContext.Claims.AddAsync(claim);
await _serviceBus.PublishAsync(event); // Blocks transaction until broker responds (dual-write problem!)
await transaction.CommitAsync();

// ✅ CORRECT - Only write to outbox in transaction, relay publishes asynchronously
using var transaction = await _dbContext.Database.BeginTransactionAsync();
await _dbContext.Claims.AddAsync(claim);
await _dbContext.Outbox.AddAsync(outboxEvent); // Fast database write
await transaction.CommitAsync(); // Transaction completes quickly
// Relay publishes asynchronously in background
```

